  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "php_hash_xxh64_unserialize",
    "file": "php-src/ext/hash/hash_xxhash.c",
    "description": "The vulnerable xxh64 HashContext unserializer accepts attacker-controlled XXH64_state_t data without validating the `memsize` invariant (`memsize < 32`). This propagates an invalid value into `XXH64_update`; with `memsize == 70`, the expression `32 - state->memsize` wraps as an unsigned 32-bit value to 4294967258, which is passed to `XXH_memcpy`, causing a huge out-of-bounds read (and an out-of-bounds destination offset). The required fix is algorithm-specific validation in `php_hash_xxh64_unserialize` after generic spec decoding; the current source's `ctx->s.memsize < 32` check represents that validation.",
    "conditions": "Supply a serialized `HashContext` selecting algorithm `xxh64`, serialization magic 2 (`PHP_HASH_SERIALIZE_MAGIC_SPEC`), and a structurally valid 22-integer state array matching `PHP_XXH64_SPEC` (`qqqqqqqqqllq`), but set array element 18\u2014the decoded 32-bit `XXH64_state_t.memsize`\u2014to 32 or greater (70 in this PoV). The harness unserializes the bytes after `|`, then passes the bytes before `|` to `hash_update`; here the delimiter is first, so the update length is zero. The corrupted nonzero memsize reaches `XXH64_update`, where `32 - memsize` underflows and becomes the oversized memcpy length."
  },
